  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "I thought of an idea that has been done in various non-VR areas, however, considering facial tracking for VR isn't that far away, I Would love to see both Webcam-based desktop head tracking, and the equivilant of that for VR to be a thing, using blendshapes (sort of like visemes), however instead of detecting sound input, it detects the input from the facial tracking system, and blends between various facial expressions... this has been done in GMOD funny enough...\nPS: I personally don't see this being a thing until way later, although this would help my sense of awkwardness when around desktop users, and how lifeless they look most of the time...",
